 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# ASCII Render\n\nA scene redrawn as text, one character per cell chosen by the cell's brightness, in green ink or in the scene's own colours. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a stat and a bar chart; label, number and bars from variables), not over the host video.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3.0 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene should arrive out of text, or read as a terminal rendering of itself: developer-facing intros, a dashboard reduced to characters.\n- The scene is high contrast, since the glyph ramp follows brightness and flat mid-tones give flat text.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The ASCII should only cover the cut between two scenes: use ascii-dissolve.\n- The scene has fine detail or small type that must stay readable: a glyph cell keeps only its average brightness.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Deploys this week\"\n- value (string): Value, default \"2,481\"\n- bars (string): Bars, default \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"\n- accent (color): Highlight, default \"#a1eebd\"\n- glyph_size (number, 10-64): Glyph size, default 26\n- charset (string): Charset, default \" .:-=+*#%@\"\n- colored (boolean): Source colour, default false\n- ink (color): Ink, default \"#9dff9d\"\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Intensity, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  ASCII Render\n\n  A scene redrawn as ASCII: one character per cell, picked from a brightness ramp. The scene\n  here is a stat and a bar chart.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/ascii-render/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  remocn captures its React children with the HTML-in-Canvas API, which a render machine does\n  not have. This block draws remocn's preview scene (a stat and a bar chart) (text and colours from the variables) on a\n  2D canvas and runs remocn's fragment shader over it, so it applies the look to its own content,\n  not to the host video behind it.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"ascii-render\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Label\", \"description\": \"Small caption above the number in the sample scene.\", \"default\": \"Deploys this week\"}, {\"id\": \"value\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Value\", \"description\": \"The big number in the sample scene.\", \"default\": \"2,481\"}, {\"id\": \"bars\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Bars\", \"description\": \"Bar heights as percentages, separated by commas (up to 12); the last bar is highlighted.\", \"default\": \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Highlight\", \"description\": \"Colour of the last bar.\", \"default\": \"#a1eebd\"}, {\"id\": \"glyph_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Glyph size\", \"description\": \"Height of one character cell. Pixel sizes are for a 1280×720 frame and scale with the frame.\", \"default\": 26, \"min\": 10, \"max\": 64, \"step\": 2, \"unit\": \"px\"}, {\"id\": \"charset\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Charset\", \"description\": \"Characters from dark to light; a space is blank. Keep at least two.\", \"default\": \" .:-=+*#%@\"}, {\"id\": \"colored\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Source colour\", \"description\": \"Colour each character from the scene instead of one ink.\", \"default\": false}, {\"id\": \"ink\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Ink\", \"description\": \"Colour of the characters when Source colour is off.\", \"default\": \"#9dff9d\"}, {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Intensity\", \"description\": \"0 shows the scene, 1 shows only characters.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Characters stay sharp at 0.75; lower renders faster but softens them.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>ASCII Render</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .asc-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .asc-canvas,\n        .asc-scene {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .asc-scene {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .asc-off .asc-canvas {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .asc-off .asc-fb {\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"ascii-render\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"asc-clip\" class=\"asc-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"asc-scene0\" class=\"asc-scene asc-fb\"></canvas>\n          <canvas id=\"asc-canvas\" class=\"asc-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"ascii-render\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"asc-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"asc-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#ffffff\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Deploys this week\"}, {\"id\": \"value\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"2,481\"}, {\"id\": \"bars\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"default\": \"#a1eebd\"}, {\"id\": \"glyph_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 26, \"min\": 10, \"max\": 64}, {\"id\": \"charset\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \" .:-=+*#%@\"}, {\"id\": \"colored\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"default\": false}, {\"id\": \"ink\", \"type\": \"color\", \"default\": \"#9dff9d\"}, {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else if (d.type === \"enum\") V[d.id] = d.options.indexOf(raw) >= 0 ? raw : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" && raw.trim() ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var res = V.resolution;\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * res));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * res));\n            var sceneCanvases = [\"asc-scene0\"].map(function (id) {\n              var el = document.getElementById(id);\n              el.width = cw;\n              el.height = ch;\n              return el;\n            });\n\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var MONO = \"'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\";\n            var INK = \"#f2f2f2\";\n            var MUTED = \"#8b8f9a\";\n            var TONES = [\"#a1eebd\", \"#ffb38e\", \"#d4b3ff\"];\n            var S = Math.min(W / 940, H / 720);\n            function setFont(ctx, weight, size, family) { ctx.font = weight + \" \" + size + \"px \" + family; }\n            function fitFont(ctx, text, maxWidth, weight, size, family) {\n              setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width;\n              if (w > maxWidth) { size *= maxWidth / w; setFont(ctx, weight, size, family); }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function setSpacing(ctx, px) { if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = px + \"px\"; }\n            function wrapLines(ctx, text, maxWidth) {\n              var words = String(text).split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n              var lines = [];\n              var line = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (word) {\n                var next = line ? line + \" \" + word : word;\n                if (line && ctx.measureText(next).width > maxWidth) { lines.push(line); line = word; }\n                else line = next;\n              });\n              if (line) lines.push(line);\n              return lines;\n            }\n            function pairs(text, max) {\n              return String(text).split(\";\")\n                .map(function (row) { return row.split(\"|\").map(function (part) { return part.trim(); }); })\n                .filter(function (row) { return row[0]; })\n                .slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function begin(ctx, cw, ch, fill) {\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = fill;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n            }\n\n\n            // Sample scene \"A\": a stat and a bar chart (remocn's CanvasSceneA), laid out for any frame size.\n            var barValues = String(V.bars).split(\",\").map(function (n) { return Math.min(100, Math.max(4, Number(n) || 0)); }).slice(0, 12);\n            if (!barValues.length) barValues = [32, 51, 43, 68, 57, 86, 64, 100];\n            function drawA(canvas) {\n              var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n              begin(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, \"#0a0a0a\");\n              var s = S, pad = 96 * s, inner = W - pad * 2;\n              var labelH = 41 * s, valueSize = 152 * s, barsH = 190 * s;\n              var total = labelH + 6 * s + valueSize + 52 * s + barsH;\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.fillStyle = MUTED;\n              fitFont(ctx, V.label, inner, 400, 34 * s, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(V.label, pad, y + labelH / 2);\n              y += labelH + 6 * s;\n              ctx.fillStyle = INK;\n              setSpacing(ctx, -0.04 * valueSize);\n              fitFont(ctx, V.value, inner, 600, valueSize, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(V.value, pad, y + valueSize / 2);\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n              y += valueSize + 52 * s;\n              var n = barValues.length;\n              var bs = Math.min(1, inner / ((n * 74 + (n - 1) * 16) * s));\n              var bw = 74 * s * bs, gap = 16 * s * bs, base = y + barsH;\n              barValues.forEach(function (v, i) {\n                var h = barsH * v / 100;\n                ctx.fillStyle = i === n - 1 ? V.accent : \"#23262e\";\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.roundRect(pad + i * (bw + gap), base - h, bw, h, 10 * s * bs);\n                ctx.fill();\n              });\n            }\n\n            function drawScenes() {\n              drawA(sceneCanvases[0]);\n            }\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\n\nuniform sampler2D u_scene;\nuniform sampler2D u_atlas;\nuniform vec2 u_cell;\nuniform float u_glyph_count;\nuniform float u_colored;\nuniform vec3 u_ink;\nuniform float u_intensity;\n\nin vec2 v_uv;\nout vec4 outColor;\n\nconst int TAPS = 3;\n\nvec4 cellAverage(vec2 center, vec2 cell) {\n  vec4 sum = vec4(0.0);\n  for (int y = 0; y < TAPS; y++) {\n    for (int x = 0; x < TAPS; x++) {\n      vec2 offset = (vec2(float(x), float(y)) + 0.5) / float(TAPS) - 0.5;\n      sum += texture(u_scene, center + offset * cell);\n    }\n  }\n  return sum / float(TAPS * TAPS);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec2 cell = max(u_cell, vec2(0.001));\n  vec2 origin = floor(v_uv / cell) * cell;\n  vec4 sampled = cellAverage(origin + cell * 0.5, cell);\n\n  float luma = dot(sampled.rgb, vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114));\n  float index = min(floor(luma * u_glyph_count), u_glyph_count - 1.0);\n\n  vec2 local = clamp((v_uv - origin) / cell, 0.008, 0.992);\n  float mask =\n    texture(u_atlas, vec2((index + local.x) / u_glyph_count, local.y)).r;\n\n  vec3 glyph = mix(u_ink, sampled.rgb, u_colored) * mask;\n  vec4 source = texture(u_scene, v_uv);\n  float amount = clamp(u_intensity, 0.0, 1.0);\n\n  outColor = vec4(\n    mix(source.rgb, glyph, amount),\n    mix(source.a, max(mask, sampled.a), amount)\n  );\n}`;\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            var extraUpload = function () {};\n            var frameFn = function () {};\n            var texUnits = [];\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              function makeTexture(unit) {\n                var texture = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                return texture;\n              }\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              [\"u_scene\", \"u_atlas\"].forEach(function (name, unit) {\n                makeTexture(unit);\n                gl.uniform1i(u(name), unit);\n              });\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_aspect\"), W / H);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              var timeLoc = u(\"u_time\");\n              upload = function () {\n                sceneCanvases.forEach(function (el, unit) {\n                  gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                  gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, el);\n                });\n                extraUpload();\n              };\n\n              var rawCharset = typeof vars.charset === \"string\" && vars.charset.length > 1 ? vars.charset : \" .:-=+*#%@\";\n              var charset = Array.from(rawCharset).slice(0, 64);\n              var CELL_W = 24, CELL_H = 44;\n              var atlas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n              atlas.width = CELL_W * charset.length;\n              atlas.height = CELL_H;\n              extraUpload = function () {\n                var actx = atlas.getContext(\"2d\");\n                actx.fillStyle = \"#000000\";\n                actx.fillRect(0, 0, atlas.width, atlas.height);\n                actx.fillStyle = \"#ffffff\";\n                actx.font = Math.round(CELL_H * 0.74) + \"px 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', monospace\";\n                actx.textAlign = \"center\";\n                actx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n                charset.forEach(function (c, i) { actx.fillText(c, i * CELL_W + CELL_W / 2, CELL_H / 2); });\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE1);\n                gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, atlas);\n              };\n              var glyph = V.glyph_size * S;\n              gl.uniform2f(u(\"u_cell\"), (glyph * 0.545) / W, glyph / H);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_glyph_count\"), charset.length);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_colored\"), V.colored ? 1 : 0);\n              var ink = rgb(V.ink);\n              gl.uniform3f(u(\"u_ink\"), ink[0], ink[1], ink[2]);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_intensity\"), V.intensity);\n\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, frame / 30);\n                frameFn(frame, frame / 30);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"asc-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scenes are redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScenes();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"500 30px Geist\", \"600 44px Geist\", \"400 44px 'Geist Mono'\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); }\n            }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "458d88cfdcf8bab4398bc2a267fd67e1dded36bd5999f70e36f6cbb5ed153ef1",
